{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>To shedim.</b> Because they plunder a person's mind, they are called shedim." "<b>They did not know them.</b> Of HaKadosh Baruch Hu it is said ״וידע אלקים״, ״כי ידעתי את מכאוביו״, but as for the abominations — they did not know them in their distress, and they did not leave them anything. And why did they not know them? Because they are <b>new</b> and <b>came recently</b> — yesterday their maker carved them." "<b>Your fathers did not know them.</b> Your fathers did not take note of them and did not concern themselves with them — like the idiom of פוקד עון, which is translated מסער."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:06.097498637Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}